purpose: How does a first-time adopter set up the standard without breaking non-interactive use?

Records the decision to add engsys setup as a seven-step guided adoption with per-step confirmation, while other commands stay non-interactive, plus init --dry-run.
Translated from Korean to English as a frozen record; the step order, --yes and no-terminal behavior, failure output rules and the docs check warning change are preserved.
Headings mapped to Decision / Context and constraints / Rationale and alternatives / Consequences.
Commands and the ADR 0007 link kept verbatim; no Korean literals retained.

